[hermes:err-live] ### milvus-io/milvus#51694 — fix: bind segment-derived resources to published state
[hermes:err-live] - State: `OPEN` · Closing-link from PR: no · Source: `cross`
[hermes:err-live] - URL: https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/pull/51694
[hermes:err-live] - Author: xiaofan-luan
[hermes:err-live] - Labels: kind/bug, size/XXL, approved, dco-passed
[hermes:err-live] #### Issue body
[hermes:err-live] issue: #51693
[hermes:err-live] ## What changed
[hermes:err-live] - Bind sealed-segment GEOMETRY caches and TEXT LOB reader handles to `PublishedSegmentState::RuntimeResourceState`, so old published snapshots retain the resources needed to interpret their data.
[hermes:err-live] - Replace the capacity-based `TextColumnCache` with reference-counted `SharedTextLobReader` handles. A global weak registry deduplicates readers by LOB path but owns no reader and applies no capacity/LRU eviction.
[hermes:err-live] - Acquire partition TEXT readers only for loaded internal V3 TEXT columns; schema-only and external TEXT fields do not create readers.
[hermes:err-live] - Keep growing-segment TEXT spillover/remote-reader representation boundaries and GEOMETRY caches in lifetime-safe shared resource state, including field-drop cleanup.
[hermes:err-live] - Return schema snapshots through `SchemaPtr` and have each expression capture the published schema snapshot at construction, so an in-flight expression keeps the schema of the segment state it started on.
[hermes:err-live] - Preserve structured storage error categories across the TEXT reader boundary: storage-transient code `2045` remains retriable, while permanent storage code `2044` remains non-retriable.
[hermes:err-live] - Add regression tests for sealed/growing resource lifetime, reader sharing and release, GEOMETRY ownership, TEXT representation boundaries, and storage error propagation.
[hermes:err-live] ## Why
[hermes:err-live] Several query-visible resources were derived from segment data but lived in independent global caches or mutable members. During reopen, replacement, or drop, the published data and those resources could therefore have different ownership lifetimes.
[hermes:err-live] The fix makes the published/runtime state the strong owner of derived resources. Shared readers are deduplicated for reuse, but their lifetime is controlled only by segment/query references rather than an unrelated process-wide capacity limit.
[hermes:err-live] ## Scope
[hermes:err-live] This PR fixes ownership and lifetime for resources derived from segment data — GEOMETRY caches, TEXT LOB readers, growing-segment representation state, and each expression's schema snapshot.
[hermes:err-live] The expression-result cache key stays generation-free (`{segment_id, predicate}`, validated by row_count). Instead of adding a generation, a reopen that **replaces existing row data** — compaction rewriting a column's parquet, or an external-manifest refresh, both of which can change a value while keeping the segment id and row count — drops that segment's cached filter bitsets (`LoadDiff::ReplacesExistingFieldData` → `InvalidateExprCacheAfterReopen`) **as `committer.Publish`'s `while_locked` hook**: after the new state is stored but before the publish lease reopens the read gate. The gate has already drained in-flight readers (their stale writes landed) and blocks new readers until the erase completes, so no query can read the freshly published data and still hit the pre-reopen bitmap — erasing *after* the lease released would leave exactly that window (P1 caught in review). Add-only reopens (new fields / indexes over unchanged values) keep the still-correct cache. This satisfies the same-row-count acceptance in #51693 without a generation in the key.
[hermes:err-live] It also does not implement the complete per-operation sealed-segment state pin tracked by #51594; access paths not covered by an explicit snapshot may still observe a later published generation between separate accessor calls.
[hermes:err-live] Related architectural direction: #51068. TEXT LOB origin: #47567 / #48783.
[hermes:err-live] ## Review fixes (2026-07-23)
[hermes:err-live] Follow-up fixes from a deep multi-agent review, squashed into this commit:
[hermes:err-live] - **Schema-only TEXT dispatch**: a TEXT field added by schema change has no manifest column and therefore no LOB reader by design; `get_raw_data` and `CreateTextIndexWithSchema` now dispatch on reader presence (no reader = plain string column) instead of hard-asserting, so adding a nullable / `enable_match` TEXT field no longer fails queries or segment reopen. Regression tests added for both paths.
[hermes:err-live] - **Recursive `sch_mutex_` acquisition**: `SegmentGrowingImpl::Insert()` holds `sch_mutex_` shared…
