[review] This PR binds segment-derived resources (GEOMETRY caches, TEXT LOB readers, schema snapshots) to published segment state so old snapshots retain the resources needed to interpret their data. It replaces the global `SimpleGeometryCacheManager` and capacity-based `TextColumnCache` with segment-owned `shared_ptr`-based lifetime, adds schema snapshot capture in expressions, fixes a `std::shared_mutex` recursive-lock UB, and invalidates the expression-result cache during data-replacing reopens via a carefully ordered `while_locked` publish hook. The diff is large (41 files, +3701/−1497) but systematic and well-tested. No blocking defects found.
